  "details": "When facing certain angles in worlds, all images in the menu can appear overexposed as if world lighting is affecting them.\n\nI can reproduce this in many worlds, but for reproducing steps I'll use the default home world as an example.\n\n1. On desktop, load in the default home world and don't move position.\n\n2. Turn to face the gap above the mirror. (Image 1)\n\n3. Open menu and if the left wing is set to profile, it should be overexposed (Image 2) compared to normal (Image 3).\n\nAll other images in the menu (and sub-menus) can be overexposed as well, but the direction to face will be different depending on menu position I've noticed. The menu buttons and interface seem to also be affected by this light, but to a lesser degree.",
